  "summary": "Dynamic physics. HairRig has no inputs: its root is anchored at the origin of the rotation deformer Hair (the first deformer output), which the rotation deformer Head moves. Its outputs add to the angle of Hair (measured from gravity as seen in Head's frame), move the origin of the rotation deformer Bow, and move the vertices of the mesh Ribbon and the control points of the warp Cape by the swing's displacement, with per-vertex weights. FrameRig has frame = Head, so its gravity turns with Head (frame angle = HeadAngle); its root is anchored at Head's origin. Turning the head to 30 degrees swings the chains; after a reset, the chains rest: Hair receives -30 degrees (it keeps hanging straight down), FrameRig outputs 30 degrees, and the displacements are 0.",
